ion:** You must reject a filename once it contains more than two decimal digits. Keep the dot, extension, and leading-letter checks unchanged.\\n\\n4. **Count Dots**\\n   - Count the number of dots in `file_name` using `file_name.count(\'.\')`. If the count is not exactly 1, return `\'No\'`.\\n\\n5. **Split by Dot**\\n   - Split `file_name` by the dot using `file_name.split(\'.\')`. Ensure there are exactly two parts: `prefix` and `suffix`.\\n\\n6. **Validate Prefix**\\n   - Check if `prefix` is not empty and starts with a letter (a-z or A-Z). If not, return `\'No\'`.\\n\\n7. **Validate Suffix**\\n   - Check if `suffix` is one of `[\'txt\', \'exe\', \'dll\']`. If not, return `\'No\'`.\\n\\n8. **Return Valid**\\n   - If all checks pass, return `\'Yes\'`.\\n\\n9. **Edge Cases**\\n   - Test with edge cases such as `file_name` containing leading/trailing spaces, `file_name` with multiple dots, and `file_name` with no digits.\\n\\n10. **Examples**\\n\\n   - Implement the checklist above directly and use the existing task validation suite.\\n\\n11. **Complexity**\\n    - Ensure the implementation has a time complexity of O(n) and a space complexity of O(1).\\n\\n12. **Testing**\\n    - Write additional test cases to cover all conditions and edge cases."}'}]
